message: "Please cite the Champollion protocol using this metadata; cite source editions and translators separately."
title: "Champollion protocol"
authors:
  - family-names: Berardi
    given-names: Michael
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-13"
url: "https://github.com/michael-berardi/champollion"
repository-code: "https://github.com/michael-berardi/champollion"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - translation protocol
  - source provenance
  - textual alignment
  - independent registers
  - offline verification
  - recorded review
abstract: >-
  Champollion specifies a method for storing canonical original-language sources,
  preserving source units and form, producing at least two independent direct-source
  registers, checking mechanical requirements, and retaining judgment and provenance
  records. Its Python reference implementation uses the standard library and local
  evidence without network calls at check time. Champollion does not translate texts
  or certify sense. This citation describes the CC BY 4.0 specification; the reference
  implementation is licensed separately under MIT. The version and release-date
  metadata do not constitute publication approval or a conformance claim for any work.
